{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/562679-huntsman-in-1ed","id":562679,"title":"Huntsman in 1ED","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-20T23:23:15-07:00","id":562679,"title":"Huntsman in 1ED","content":"Prepering for mine last night game for out club, I looked for antagonists in <b>Grim Fears</b> book. I read about Skin and Bones, the capture of persons, and thought to myself - &quot;damn, this must be a Huntsman in 2ED!&quot;<br /> <br /> So question is simple - <b>Did anywhere else shown up Huntsman-like fae characters in 1ED gameline to look on to what kind creeps we can find in 2ED? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:25:32-07:00","id":562700,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen or huntsmen? Cause 1E had a lot of the latter.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for the former, but I imagine we'll actually find them both unlike anything we've seen before and disturbingly familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:31:02-07:00","id":562703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/562679-huntsman-in-1ed?p=562700#post562700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen or huntsmen? Cause 1E had a lot of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the proper Huntsman were not in the 1ED. But Huntsman-like ( and just &quot;huntsman&quot; ) could be multiple, I suspect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So the latter for now, let's look. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T03:48:34-07:00","id":562846,"title":"","content":"Core book, the antagonist chapter, who had hosts of briarwolves with him, and often turnes any he cought into briarwolves as well.<br /> <br /> I run off the assumption 2e huntsman expand on this idea from 1e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:53:14-07:00","id":563426,"title":"","content":"I know it was mentioned somewhere that a scary aspect of Huntsmen in 2e is they can shapeshift into different objects to get closer to their target. There was one post made somewhere of saying a Huntsman could essentially shift into a piece of the Changeling's furniture in their home after getting rid of the original and they wouldn't know until it's too late. That the Boogeyman isn't under the bed, <i>it is the bed</i>... That's a frightening prospect.<br /> <br /> I still have images in my mind of a Huntsman taking the form of a Changeling's wardrobe and swallowing them up inside it when they go to get dressed one morning... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That it can know where their quarry is if they find a soul shard in the Hedge, I love that mechanic means Changelings are going to have to bite the bullet and go finding their soul shards in the Hedge and not stick their heads in the sand anymore, like too many did in 1e. I like this because I loved to explore the Hedge in 1e and it sucked being with a troupe where someone didn't want to touch anything to do with it with a 10 foot barge pole. I also read apparently that the soul shards slowly return back to where they were in the Hedge if removed from it. I'm hoping this doesn't happen too often (maybe the time intervals are linked to Wyrd in a similar way B:tP has Hunger intervals that change?), but more Hedge is great for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With all that in mind and bearing that I haven't touched 1e in a little while, are there any antagonists that track changelings down and shapeshift to avoid suspicion like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}